From: Fedora bc maintainers
Subject: Document the scale of multiplication results

The shipped bc manual does not say how the scale of a product is chosen.
Peios carries this Fedora documentation fix so the installed manual states
the rule bc actually applies. Only documentation changes.

Origin: vendor, Fedora bc package, bc-1.06.95-doc.patch
Forwarded: no

diff --git a/doc/bc.1 b/doc/bc.1
--- a/doc/bc.1
+++ b/doc/bc.1
@@ -174,6 +174,8 @@ The result of the expression is the sum of the two expressions.
 The result of the expression is the difference of the two expressions.
 .IP "expr * expr"
 The result of the expression is the product of the two expressions.
+If a and b are the scales of the two expressions, then the scale of the result is:
+min(a+b,max(scale,a,b))
 .IP "expr / expr"
 The result of the expression is the quotient of the two expressions.
 The scale of the result is the value of the variable \fBscale\fR.
diff --git a/doc/bc.texi b/doc/bc.texi
--- a/doc/bc.texi
+++ b/doc/bc.texi
@@ -290,6 +290,8 @@ The result of the expression is the difference of the two expressions.
 
 @item expr * expr
 The result of the expression is the product of the two expressions.
+If a and b are the scales of the two expressions, then the scale of the result is:
+min(a+b,max(@var{scale},a,b))
 
 @item expr / expr
 The result of the expression is the quotient of the two expressions.
